<pre class='metadata'>
Title: Agentic Integrity Verification Specification (AIVS) v1.0
Shortname: aivs
Level: 1
Status: CG-DRAFT
Group: aivs
URL: https://www.w3.org/community/aivs/
Editor: Jinghan Zhang, Contributed as an input strawman
Abstract: This document specifies the Agentic Integrity Verification Specification (AIVS), a portable, self-verifiable archive format for cryptographic proof of AI agent sessions. An AIVS proof bundle is a structured archive containing a SHA-256 hash-chained audit log, an Ed25519 digital signature over the chain, a machine-readable manifest, and an embedded verification script. AIVS enables any party to independently verify that every action in an agent session is accounted for and unmodified, that no actions have been inserted, deleted, or reordered, and that the session was produced by a specific cryptographic identity.
Markup Shorthands: markdown yes
</pre>

<h2 id="status">Status of This Document</h2>

This report was published by the [Agentic Integrity Verification Specification Community Group](https://www.w3.org/community/aivs/). It is not a W3C Standard nor is it on the W3C Standards Track. Please note that under the [W3C Community Contributor License Agreement (CLA)](https://www.w3.org/community/about/process/cla/) there is a limited opt-out and other conditions apply. Learn more about [W3C Community and Business Groups](https://www.w3.org/community/).

